# Project-root .env -- auto-loaded by docker compose. Copy to .env (gitignored).
# Separate from backend/.env, which holds the app's API credentials.

# --- Primary checkout ---------------------------------------------------

# Tailscale auth key for the `tailscale` sidecar.
# Generate at: Tailscale admin console -> Settings -> Keys -> Generate auth key
# Make it REUSABLE and NON-EPHEMERAL (the node must persist across restarts).
# Only used on first login -- once the tailscale_state volume holds the node
# identity, the node re-authenticates with its own key and this can be removed.
TS_AUTHKEY=

# --- Git worktree stacks ------------------------------------------------
#
# The block below is what scripts/bootstrap-worktree.sh writes into a
# worktree's root .env. The primary checkout leaves all three unset and gets
# the defaults (8086 and 3001, and no overlay). See the "Git worktrees"
# section of CLAUDE.md.
#
# Layer the worktree overlay on top of the base compose file. It gates the
# tailscale sidecar off and disables the hourly scheduler jobs.
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yaml:docker-compose.worktree.yaml
#
# The app's URL, published by proxy-vue. Default 8086.
# MYDIARY_HTTP_PORT=8087
#
# Direct access to the Vite dev server, bound to 127.0.0.1. Default 3001.
# MYDIARY_VITE_PORT=3002
#
# A worktree deliberately omits TS_AUTHKEY as well -- belt and braces
# alongside the profile gate in docker-compose.worktree.yaml.
